1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,020
Part three. The missing filing.

2
00:00:02,589 --> 00:00:04,795
Nvidia reported earnings this week,

3
00:00:04,899 --> 00:00:07,721
under interim chief executive Colette Kress,

4
00:00:08,081 --> 00:00:09,567
the former finance chief.

5
00:00:09,927 --> 00:00:10,948
On the surface:

6
00:00:11,378 --> 00:00:12,411
record numbers,

7
00:00:12,771 --> 00:00:15,720
beat expectations, raised forecast.

8
00:00:16,149 --> 00:00:18,576
But Zitron spotted what wasn't there.

9
00:00:19,145 --> 00:00:22,036
Normally, Nvidia files its quarterly report,

10
00:00:22,117 --> 00:00:24,846
the ten-Q, alongside earnings.

11
00:00:25,113 --> 00:00:26,215
This time, nothing.

12
00:00:26,889 --> 00:00:28,305
The deadline, he says,

13
00:00:28,328 --> 00:00:29,640
is December 4th,

14
00:00:29,873 --> 00:00:32,543
and Kress promised it within the coming weeks.

15
00:00:33,216 --> 00:00:35,619
Bulls say it's just extra checks during the

16
00:00:35,666 --> 00:00:37,814
investigation into Jensen Huang.

17
00:00:38,382 --> 00:00:39,857
Zitron isn't convinced:

18
00:00:39,938 --> 00:00:42,516
the scandal broke just a week before earnings,

19
00:00:42,876 --> 00:00:45,186
so the filing was likely nearly done.

20
00:00:45,674 --> 00:00:48,530
His words: we need answers from Nvidia.

21
00:00:49,307 --> 00:00:50,248
On the scandal,

22
00:00:50,283 --> 00:00:51,908
he cites the Wall Street Journal,

23
00:00:52,070 --> 00:00:54,439
which he says now puts chip sales through

24
00:00:54,474 --> 00:00:56,192
Megaspeed at around $12 billion.

25
00:00:56,761 --> 00:00:58,526
Those are reports and allegations,

26
00:00:58,560 --> 00:00:59,431
not findings.

27
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:00,790
Then his guest,

28
00:01:00,894 --> 00:01:03,773
Steve from the hardware channel Gamers Nexus,

29
00:01:03,936 --> 00:01:05,654
pulls up Nvidia's own numbers.

30
00:01:06,560 --> 00:01:09,915
Revenue booked to Singapore went from about $760

31
00:01:09,996 --> 00:01:11,749
million in one quarter

32
00:01:12,214 --> 00:01:14,605
to about $4 billion a year later.

33
00:01:15,256 --> 00:01:16,730
Over one fiscal year,

34
00:01:16,951 --> 00:01:18,390
roughly $24 billion.

35
00:01:19,040 --> 00:01:21,084
And then it vanished from the breakdown,

36
00:01:21,386 --> 00:01:24,393
after Nvidia changed how it reports revenue by

37
00:01:24,486 --> 00:01:25,008
region.

38
00:01:25,647 --> 00:01:26,738
Steve's question:

39
00:01:27,168 --> 00:01:29,234
a company that can tell when a driver

40
00:01:29,339 --> 00:01:31,545
leaks to a reviewer can't track its own

41
00:01:31,591 --> 00:01:32,207
chips?

42
00:01:33,263 --> 00:01:35,492
One more thing doesn't add up for Zitron.

43
00:01:35,980 --> 00:01:39,428
In August, Nvidia promised 70% growth next year.

44
00:01:40,101 --> 00:01:42,562
Yet the Journal reported Jensen worried about a

45
00:01:42,644 --> 00:01:44,687
glut of chip-making capacity.

46
00:01:45,256 --> 00:01:46,684
You can't easily have both.

47
00:01:47,114 --> 00:01:48,251
The board, he says,

48
00:01:48,391 --> 00:01:50,933
has made clear Jensen isn't coming back.

49
00:01:51,607 --> 00:01:53,453
So can anyone do what he did?
